 "status": "PROPOSED, awaiting owner review (2026-11-09)",
 "photo": "data/photos/anchor_front.webp",
 "coords": "photo pixels; pixel (col,row) covers [col,col+1)x[row,row+1)",
 "meaning": "Where each ear meets his head: the ear is above the line, the head below.",
 "how": "Measured crease, not guessed. A dark-groove filter (sato, sigma 4-7 px) read column by column, more than 10 px inside the outline (a cheapest-path search had followed the dark rim around the ears and was discarded). Ear (image right): one continuous crease x 611-674, y 280->290, 3-4x the groove strength of random lines on the head; joined at its inner end to the corner where the dip between the ears starts rising (572.6, 272.3), continued straight along its own direction to the ear's outer side (717.6, 307.9). Ear (image left): fainter, broken crease (x 410-425 and 470-497), anchored at the ear's outline corners: outer (376.5, 287.1) and the bottom of its step into the dip (512.9, 275.8); the small ledge belongs to the ear. The flat dip between the two (x 513-572) is the top of his head. Asymmetry (right ear's base ~20 px lower outside) left as is: real rabbit.",
